UBI provides a guaranteed income floor, allowing individuals to cover essential expenses like food, housing, and healthcare.
This financial stability reduces the risk of poverty for vulnerable populations, including the elderly, disabled, and unemployed.
By ensuring a basic income, UBI can reduce the stress and uncertainty associated with financial instability, leading to better mental and physical health outcomes.
UBI can act as a safety net during economic downturns, preventing widespread poverty and social unrest.
Studies from pilot programs show that UBI can improve overall well-being and economic participation without reducing work incentives.